WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.544
Talking money without panic is a skill.

00:00:02.544 --> 00:00:04.724
Silence after the number is normal.

00:00:04.724 --> 00:00:06.904
This lesson is about pricing conversations.

00:00:06.904 --> 00:00:08.358
Talking money without panic.

00:00:08.358 --> 00:00:10.902
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:10.902 --> 00:00:14.535
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:14.535 --> 00:00:19.986
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:23.983
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:23.983 --> 00:00:28.344
Stay practical: roleplay a price talk before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:28.664 --> 00:00:30.151
Say the price clearly.

00:00:30.151 --> 00:00:31.266
Then stop talking.

00:00:31.266 --> 00:00:32.381
Let them respond.

00:00:32.381 --> 00:00:34.982
Remember the objective: roleplay a price talk.

00:00:34.982 --> 00:00:39.071
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:39.071 --> 00:00:43.531
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:43.531 --> 00:00:47.619
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:47.619 --> 00:00:52.080
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:54.681
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:54.681 --> 00:00:56.168
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:00:56.488 --> 00:01:02.020
